  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1246 AM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nFair but warmer weather makes a return for Sunday and Monday with \nsome ridging aloft in-between storm systems. Temperatures return to \nthe mid to upper 80s for most locations that are outside from the \nHill Country with greater sunshine. The Hill Country trends more in \nthe upper 70s to low 80s. Overnight lows, though, remain warm and \nhumid, in the mid to upper 60s with low clouds arriving from the \novernight into each morning.\n\nThe latest medium range guidance remains in better alignment on the \nmid-level pattern with a storm system that will develop coming off \nthe Rockies and move into the Southern Plains during Monday into \nTuesday. This system advances a cold front through the region \nsometime during the first half of Tuesday. This front has a \ncontinued signal on bringing a potential line of showers and storms \nalong it and we'll continue to monitor for the possibility of some \nstrong storms with the combination of some adequate shear and \ninstability.\n\nModerate northwesterly winds following the front's passage helps to \nusher in a drier airmass for mid to late next week. This yields to \ncooler mornings and mild but comfortable afternoons.",
